2	
3	// End-to-end regression coverage for `alerts history` against a saved
4	// processing record whose detection-version declaration has decayed since
5	// the record was written. History must first prove — per hit record, from
6	// the record's own saved declaration — the same integrity rules a `report`
7	// query enforces before printing any alert or suppression result: exit
8	// code 1, no history JSON on stdout, an error naming the record's chain,
9	// block hash, victim tx hash, conclusion kind, conclusion type and
10	// channel plus the readable version id and the offending field, and no
11	// change to the archive. Records on another channel stay queryable.
